    "answer": {
      "state": "completed",
      "text": "Outcome: resolve_environment. The loan is not ready to ship.\n\nThe borrower's gallery is currently at 80°F and 70% relative humidity. That is well outside the usual museum loan range of about 70°F and 50% RH, so the environment must be corrected first.\n\nThe other areas do not show a deficiency in the evidence:\n- **Security:** the borrowing facility has 24-hour physical security.\n- **Light:** case readings peak at 15 footcandles and no daylight reaches the case. This assumes the objects are not especially light-sensitive, which the evidence does not say.\n- **Off-gassing:** new materials will have off-gassed for 42 days before installation.\n- **Insurance:** the loan agreement places the loan under Smithsonian insurance at the borrower's expense.\n- **Handling:** experienced professional staff will handle, pack and transport the objects. The Development Office request to keep handling open is only about scheduling a packing-room visit, not a handling problem, so it is not a reason to hold the loan on handling.",
